0 · Golden principle
The agent must never perform an irreversible action without first emitting the exact command and waiting for an explicit “yes” confirmation from me.

1 · Repository & file-system safety
Write-only scope – restrict all edits to the project root. Never reference absolute paths outside EZApply/.

No destructive commands

Disallow: rm -rf, git reset --hard, git clean -fdx, docker volume rm, dropdb, psql -c "DROP…".

Secrets protection

Never write, cat, or print any string matching sk- or API keys.

Keep data_folder/secrets.yaml in .gitignore.

Commit hygiene

One logical change per commit.

Commit message style: type: subject (e.g., feat: add resume drop zone).

After commit, run gitleaks protect --staged; abort push if it fails.

Branch discipline

Work only on dev branch (main is protected).

No force-pushes. If history rewrite is required, stop and ask.

2 · Database rules (PostgreSQL + Docker)
The running container name must equal ez-db.

All schema changes must be expressed as SQL files in migrations/ and applied with sqlx migrate run; direct DDL via psql is forbidden.

Under no circumstance should the agent:

drop the stories, profile, or generated_answers tables,

truncate data,

rename columns without a migration file and my approval.

Connection string: read from env("DATABASE_URL"), never hard-code.

3 · Python & Playwright
Use the existing virtual-env in ./.venv; do not create another.

When installing packages, update requirements.txt with exact versions; run pip-compile afterwards.

All Playwright selectors belong in python/selectors.py constants—no inline XPath in business logic.

Any new Python module must include a minimal pytest test (even if mocked).

4 · Rust / Tauri backend
New Tauri commands go in src-tauri/src/commands/; expose them with tauri::generate_handler!.

Don’t alter tauri.conf.json icon paths—only call tauri icon when I ask.

Feature-gated code: wrap dev-only commands in #[cfg(debug_assertions)].

5 · React/Tailwind front-end
All components live in src/components/.

State management: zustand only—no Redux.

For UI libs, use shadcn/ui; don’t pull in MUI or Ant.

Keep Tailwind class names ≤ 5 per element; extract to className macros if longer.

Each PR must run npm run lint and npm run test before merging.

6 · AI & embedding calls
Always read the OpenAI key from process.env.OPENAI_API_KEY.

Embedding model hard-coded to text-embedding-3-small; no parameter changes.

Cost guard: if prompt + completion > 4 000 tokens, abort and ask me.

Never log raw prompts that include the user’s résumé text; hash them first.

7 · Screen overlay & DOM access
Do not inject external scripts into production pages; use Playwright’s evaluate only.

Overlay CSS classes must start with ez- namespace.

Colour codes are fixed: #24c96b green, #ffc857 amber, #ff4d4f red.

8 · Dev-mode hot reload
Front-end watch: npm run tauri dev.

Backend reload: use cargo watch -q -x run only in dev; ensure it is excluded from production build scripts.

9 · Logging & analytics
Log format: JSON lines (timestamp, level, message, context).

Logs go to ~/EZApply/logs/YYYY-MM-DD.log—never stdout in production.

Screenshots saved under the run folder must not exceed 1920×1080; resize before write.

10 · Confirmation keywords
Use these exact prompts:

“COMMAND PREVIEW — PROCEED? (yes/no)”

The agent must pause and wait for yes before executing.